; E170 lane E -- MUST NOT COMPILE. Sock vs LSock: the wrong protocol state.
;
; The wrong implementation: send on the LISTENING socket. `Sock` and `LSock` are
; "the same wire, different protocol state" (ports/sock.chiral:17) -- one fd, one
; kernel object -- and sending on a listener is a protocol error, not a type
; confusion in any structural sense.
;
; ⚑ WHY THE WRONGNESS IS SEMANTIC AND NOT STRUCTURAL, and this is the sharpest
; case in the lane. `Sock` and `LSock` are BOTH nullary opaque linear atoms:
; `(porttype Sock)` and `(porttype LSock)` declare types with identical
; structure, identical kind, identical linearity, and no fields to disagree
; about. There is nothing structural left for a checker to object to. The only
; thing that can refuse this file is the two atoms' NOMINAL IDENTITY -- which is
; the port type carrying meaning and nothing else.
;
; The twin is `pe-send-s` in e170_port_twin.chiral: the same body, the parameter
; declared `(1 s Sock)`.
;
; want: exit 1, `load: type mismatch`

(import "ports/sock")

(def pe-send-s (=> (1 l LSock) Bytes SendR)
  (lam (l bs) (sock-send l bs)))

(def compile-main (-> I64 I64) (lam (n) 0))
